# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — blueprint §5.14.
#
# Nothing in this file may ever contain a real secret. It documents the shape of
# the environment, not its contents.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Matches docker-compose.yml. Port 5433, not 5432 — see the comment there.
# Production points at Supabase's pooled connection string instead.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://naitikos:naitikos@localhost:5433/naitikos

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase and auth
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `apps/web/lib/env.ts` validates all of these at startup and its failure
# message says to copy this file — so until 7 September 2026 it named a file
# that documented one of the six variables it needs.

# The project URL the browser talks to. Public by design: it appears in the
# CSP `connect-src`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# The anon key. Public, and safe **only because of migration 0004** — RLS is
# enabled and unpolicied on every table and the PostgREST grants are revoked,
# so a holder of this key reaches a database that returns nothing. Remove that
# migration and this line becomes a full data breach.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# The origin this deployment serves. Explicit rather than read from the request
# `Host` header, which an attacker controls — a CSRF check against an
# attacker-supplied expected origin is not a check.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# The allowlist (§5.4). Comma-separated; normally one address.
AUTH_ALLOWLIST=you@example.com

# Service-role key. `lib/env.ts` marks it `.optional()`, so the app boots
# without it. It bypasses RLS entirely, which is why it is not set by default.
#
# **It is no longer unused.** Corrected 8 September 2026: this block previously
# said "deliberately unused today". `createSupabaseStorageProvider` throws at
# construction without it, and `POST /api/media/uploads` constructs it on the
# live path — so on a deployment with media capture in use, leaving this unset
# means every photograph and document upload answers 500. Set it or accept that,
# but make it a decision. See docs/runbooks/deployment.md §4 and §12.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI (§10)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic API key. Genuinely optional: `transportFromEnv` returns null when it
# is absent, `/ask` degrades to the unconfigured transport with a message saying
# the AI layer is off, and `/settings/ai` reports `transportConfigured: false`.
# Every figure in the application is computed without it.
#
# Read only on the server — `lib/platform/ask.ts` and `lib/platform/settings.ts`
# — and deliberately NOT in `lib/env.ts`, so it is not validated at startup and
# an absent key is a configuration rather than a crash. It must never be given a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix; that would inline a billable credential into the browser
# bundle.
#
# Documented here on 8 September 2026 because it was the one variable the
# application reads that this file did not name — see docs/runbooks/deployment.md §4.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
